# WeCreate — environment variables
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in what you need. Every value below is optional
# for local development: with none of them set the application runs on the
# bundled fixture content and the acceptance suite passes.
#
# Secrets are server-only. Anything prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ is compiled into the
# browser bundle, so nothing sensitive may ever carry that prefix.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deployment identity
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Absolute origin of this deployment. Used for canonical URLs, Open Graph, the
# sitemap and the Studio's preview target. Inferred from Vercel when unset.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Only the production deployment is crawlable. Leave unset on staging and
# preview so they stay out of search results.
# WECREATE_ALLOW_INDEXING=true

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Managed Content provider
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# `sanity` or `fixture`. Unset means: Sanity when a project id is configured,
# the bundled fixture content otherwise.
# WECREATE_CONTENT_PROVIDER=sanity

# Sanity project. Local, staging and production each use their own dataset.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_PROJECT_ID=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_DATASET=production
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_API_VERSION=2026-08-01

# Server-only. Grants read access to unpublished documents; required for
# preview. Never expose to the browser.
# SANITY_API_READ_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Video platform
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Mux's environment key, for aggregate playback quality and engagement
# measurement (ADR-0007). Public by design and anonymous: no viewer identity is
# ever attached to it. Playback works without it; only the measurement stops.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MUX_ENV_KEY=

# Mux's API access token is NOT an environment variable. The Studio's video
# plugin stores it in the dataset (document `secrets.mux`), so each environment's
# dataset carries its own — set it once from the Studio's video tool.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Commerce data plane
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# `supabase`, `fixture`, or unset. Unset means: Supabase when SUPABASE_URL is
# configured, and no data plane at all otherwise — the site runs, the Boutique
# reports that nothing has an activated file, and /commerce says it is not
# configured. The fixture is never selected by inference: it ships published
# staff credentials for the acceptance suite, so it has to be asked for.
# WECREATE_COMMERCE_PROVIDER=supabase

# Supabase project. Server-only, both of them: Supabase is never contacted from
# the browser (ADR-0003), so neither value carries the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.
# Local, staging and production use separate projects, buckets and keys.
# SUPABASE_URL=https://<project>.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# There is deliberately no service role key. The back office signs in as the
# individual member of staff doing the work, so Postgres applies the policies in
# supabase/migrations/ against a real identity — a key that bypassed row-level
# security would make them decorative.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Payments
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# `fedapay`, `fixture`, or unset. Unset means: FedaPay when FEDAPAY_SECRET_KEY
# is configured, and no payment provider at all otherwise — the site runs, the
# Boutique still works, and the checkout says out loud that online payment is
# not open yet. The fixture is never selected by inference: it sends buyers to
# an address that does not exist, so it has to be asked for.
# WECREATE_PAYMENT_PROVIDER=fedapay

# FedaPay's secret API key. Server-only, and the reason there is no
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FEDAPAY_* anything: transactions are created on the server and the
# buyer leaves for FedaPay's own hosted page, so no browser here ever holds a
# payment credential. Staging and production use separate FedaPay environments,
# separate keys and separate webhooks.
# FEDAPAY_SECRET_KEY=

# `sandbox` (the default) or `live`. Switching to live is the Commerce Launch
# Gate's own irreversible decision and belongs to a named WeCreate owner — see
# README.md, "Before this goes live". Nothing in the repository selects it.
# FEDAPAY_ENVIRONMENT=sandbox

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Preview and cache revalidation
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Lets a non-Sanity client open a preview session at
# /api/draft/enable?secret=…&path=/. Sanity's Presentation tool authenticates
# with the editor's own session instead and does not need this.
# WECREATE_PREVIEW_SECRET=

# Bearer token accepted by POST /api/revalidate, for operators and for
# deployments not backed by a Sanity webhook.
# WECREATE_REVALIDATE_SECRET=

# Shared secret configured on the Sanity webhook. The request signature is
# verified against the raw body.
# SANITY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Acceptance tests
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Set by playwright.config.ts; listed here for reference only. Each test hook
# answers 404 unless WECREATE_TEST_HOOKS=1 *and* its own provider is the fixture
# — the content hook needs WECREATE_CONTENT_PROVIDER=fixture, the commerce hook
# needs WECREATE_COMMERCE_PROVIDER=fixture — so neither can be reached on a
# deployment backed by a real Sanity project or a real Supabase project.
#
# WECREATE_TEST_HOOKS=1
# WECREATE_CONTENT_PROVIDER=fixture
# WECREATE_FIXTURE_FILE=/absolute/path/to/content.json
# WECREATE_COMMERCE_PROVIDER=fixture
# WECREATE_COMMERCE_FIXTURE_FILE=/absolute/path/to/commerce.json
# WECREATE_PAYMENT_PROVIDER=fixture
#
# The provider-contract smoke test (`pnpm test:contract`) is the one suite that
# talks to a real service. It skips itself unless FEDAPAY_SECRET_KEY is set, and
# refuses to run at all unless FEDAPAY_ENVIRONMENT is the sandbox.
